      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e field names are not encoded in protobuf (but field numbers are), so I think this change is safe.\n\nThat is true, but my comment was more in spirt of starting a conversation around \"should we ensure that we don\u0027t do non-compatible changes to our storage schema\"\n\n\u003e But a T -\u003e U OTA is going to invalidate the instance anyway.\n\nOh, good to know. Then we shouldn\u0027t care about this :)",
      "parentUuid": "4f659b79_68ab30cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 1
      },
